From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 02:50:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: add the camera PMIC

Add the camera power management IC and the i2c bus it sits on, the first
piece of camera support on this device.

The vendor tree puts it on qupv3_se7_i2c (i2c@4c84000, mainline's i2c7),
which mainline leaves disabled and without a pinctrl state. The pins come
from the vendor pinctrl (blair-pinctrl.dtsi: qupv3_se7_i2c_active, gpio27
and gpio28, function qup11_f1) and mainline's pinctrl-sm6375 already
defines that function for exactly those pins.

The part is NOT the "semi,wl2868c" at 0x2f that the vendor DT declares.
Probed on the device, it answers at 0x35 with CHIP_REV 0x01, which the
vendor's own driver decodes as a FAN53870 -- it tries 0x2f first and
retries at 0x35 for precisely this reason, since Motorola shipped three
pin-compatible parts under one node.

It also has an active-high enable pin on TLMM 33 and does not ACK its
address at all while that is low, which is why i2cdetect finds nothing on
a freshly booted phone.

The three LDOs named here are the ones the vendor sensor node uses for the
main camera (cam_vdig/cam_vana/cam_vio from ldo1/ldo4/ldo7); the voltages
are the vendor's rounded to the chip's 8 mV step. The remaining four LDOs
are left for whoever adds the other three sensors.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -455,6 +455,49 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Camera PMIC. The vendor device tree declares a "semi,wl2868c" at 0x2f
+ * (rhodep-wl2868c.dtsi), but the part actually fitted answers at 0x35 with
+ * CHIP_REV 0x01, which its own driver decodes as a FAN53870. The vendor
+ * driver probes 0x2f first and retries at 0x35 for exactly this reason.
+ *
+ * The chip does not ACK until its enable pin is asserted, hence the GPIO.
+ */
+&i2c7 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&qup_i2c7_default>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	cam_pmic: regulator@35 {
+		compatible = "onnn,fan53870";
+		reg = <0x35>;
+		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 33 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_pmic_en_default>;
+
+		regulators {
+			cam_vdig: LDO1 {
+				regulator-name = "cam_vdig";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1056000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1056000>;
+			};
+
+			cam_vana: LDO4 {
+				regulator-name = "cam_vana";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <2804000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <2804000>;
+			};
+
+			cam_vio: LDO7 {
+				regulator-name = "cam_vio";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1804000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1804000>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c8 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
@@ -1489,3 +1532,19 @@
 		qcom,sd-lines = <0>;
 	};
 };
+
+&tlmm {
+	cam_pmic_en_default: cam-pmic-en-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio33";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	qup_i2c7_default: qup-i2c7-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio27", "gpio28";
+		function = "qup11_f1";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+};
